MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_001: Ah... Mm... Urgh...
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_002: Stay your distance! Please, get away from me while\nyou can!
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_003: A-ah...
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_004: There you are. I should have known you would get\nthe civilians away safely as well. Thank you.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_005: I believe the worst of it is over. I should be \nalright now.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_006: <NCA>"May I ask what happened?"
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_007: <NCB>"Was it your bloodmark?"
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_008: <ACA>I was at the mercy of the bloodmark within me.\nWhat you saw often happens after battle.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_009: <ACB>Yes... This tends to happen after battle.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_010: On one hand, the crest offers untold strength and a\nlong life. On the other...well, you saw the other.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_011: There's a feeling that never leaves, that eventually\nI'll just fall apart and disappear.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_012: <NCA>"Ursula...are you alright?"
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_013: I fear the bloodmark's power is too useful to keep\ncaged away like I have. Especially now.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_014: My ancestor, Maurice, was addicted to this power.\nAnd in the end, he let it turn him into a monster.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_015: I can't say when, but I'm certain that fate will come \nfor me one day as well...
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_016: So, to that end, I need you to promise me something.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_017: If I do begin the beast transformation, could you...\nput an end to me first?
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_018: Ngh...
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_019: My entire family was killed because of this mark. If I\nhadn't fled when I did, it would have killed me too.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_020: But then I met Talimun. He said even if I turned into\na beast, he'd just use me to attract customers.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_021: I'm sure that doesn't sound as sweet as it felt.\nBut those words of his saved me.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_022: I know Talimun is a man of his word. Be I human or\nmonster, to him, I'm always just Ursula.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_023: Talimun may no longer be with us...but his words \nwill forever live in the memory of those he loved.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_024: "Even if Ursula turns beast, you'll answer to me if \nyou treat her as anything less than manager, clear?"
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_025: So...maybe now you understand why I can't let\nthat happen.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_026: You're the only person I can ask, really. So when\nthe time comes to stop me, please...
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_027: <NCA>"OK...I understand."
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_028: <NCB>"I will. I promise you."
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_A_029: Good. I'm trusting in you, Promised One.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S_001: You're alright! What a relief. You leaving wasn't a \npart of our promise.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S_002: And we merchants are rather strict with our word.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S_003: <NCA>"You're angry, aren't you?"
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S_004: <NCB>"I'm sorry, Ursula."
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S_005: <ACA>Angry? Why, livid would be more like it...\nJoking. I'm relieved, if anything.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S_006: <ACB>I was hoping to stay mad, but you do make it hard...\nI'm just happy to see you again.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S_007: When you didn't return, I was so ready to turn my\nback on prayer—on believing entirely.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S_008: How does one forgive a goddess who abandons her\nheroes? I'm grateful I was wrong.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S_009: Look at all this. The sight of a world without war.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S_010: Own this view, Promised One. This peace is yours.\nIt would be a shame to die without seeing it.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S_011: <NCA>"Right as always, Ursula."
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S_012: <NCB>"It's beautiful."
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S_013: Perhaps now, we can finally get back to business.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S_014: What if I told you I have decided to stay with the\nVandahl Trading Company for now?
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S_015: A-ah!
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S_016: Like I said, we merchants keep our promises. You\ncould stand to learn a thing or two from us.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S_017: <NCA>"I knew you were angry..."
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S_018: Maybe... But I was able to emerge from all of this\nwhile still remaining myself...
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S_019: So, thank you. Your promise granted me more\ncourage than you will ever know.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S_020: <RSDS>I know your path will lead you to those who still\nneed saving.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S_021: But if you're ever in need, know you have allies\nat Vandahl Trading.
MID_SE_Ism_Urs_S_022: Dagda gave me a place to call home. You have a\nmerchant's word that I'll always give you the same.